```

The requirement is explicit: the `C:map` block must **trail all cached C:event blocks**. If a caller places the cache breakpoint on `C:event:N`, the map—which grows on every file edit—must ride *after* that marker in the uncached tail. If the map sits *ahead* of the breakpoint (as it did in v5.5), every edit rewrites bytes before the cached prefix, voiding lookups on the append-only event stream behind it (the volatile-bit law, measured as FM-7 in iter8-rep1: cacheRead pinned 6,568 while cacheWrite re-billed 10.8k→16.3k every edit turn). The fix was the map relocation itself; the comment documents why.

